WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.200
This is the studio, where teams build public services.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.800
Not from scratch, but from the same parts, then checked and approved.

NOTE What the vendor needs

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.200
Start from what a food vendor needs to do:

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.500
apply, have the hygiene certificate checked,

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.400
pay the fee, and get the permit.

NOTE The same parts

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.400
Each step is built from the same parts,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.200
the ones public services need again and again,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.000
using national sign-in and payments already in place.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.800
Only the parts this service needs.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.600
Together they form one configuration, not new code.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.100
Edit it visually, with an AI assistant, or by hand.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.600
Code only where it's needed.

NOTE Checks and approval

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.000
Every part checks its own settings,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.600
and if they don't fit together, it can't be handed over.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.400
An approver at the council signs.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.000
Only then is it handed over.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.400
Its catalogue entry comes from the same file.

NOTE A later change

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.300
Later, the council adds a site inspection.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.600
The AI assistant proposes the change.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.800
The checks catch what was left behind.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.400
Approved again, version two is handed over.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.600
A reviewed edit, not a new project.

NOTE Close

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.000
Built from the same parts.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.800
Approved before handover.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.600
Registry Stack.
